Expected value (Mean): what the one value you get after many trials.
Ex. for dice what is the one value that is average of all values / all trials
	Calculation: 1*⅙ + 2*⅙  + 3*⅙ + 4*⅙ + 5*⅙  + 6*⅙ = 3.5


This is calculated theoretically that’s why it is called expected value of guaranteed value.
You get very near to this value in real life after millions of trials.

Mean tell us the center.

— — 

Variance = Breadth / spread of sample space 
Not the numbers of outcomes in sample space but distance between them.
Variance : {10, 25, 40} > {20, 25, 30}, both have same mean but 1st has more variance

Formula: 1. Var(X) = E[(X − E[X])² ] 
	    2. Var(X) = E(X)² − (E[X])² ]
		Both are same

Steps to calculate:
Find the mean.
Compute each value's distance from the mean.
Square the distances.
Take the expected value of those squared distances.



