JOINT PROBABILITY: mix probability of two or more variables. (AND not OR)

MARGINAL PROBABILITY: probability of only one variable (OR not AND)

CONDITIONAL PROBABILITY: probability where one or more variables are fixed, and we need probability of other variable(s) at that fixed value of fixed variable(s).

Mutually exclusive events: THe events which cannot co-exist

P(A∣B) is read as “the probability of event A dependent on B

Bay’s theorem: probability inverter;  P(B|A) → P(A|B)



One Variable → Probability Distribution → Joint Probability → Marginal Probability → Conditional Probability → Independent / Dependent Events → Mutually Exclusive Events → Bayes' Theorem


